---
description: Flutter presentation versus business-logic separation
globs: flutter_app/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Presentation code must not call repositories or Dio directly.

Presentation should communicate through the established Riverpod
providers/controllers/use cases.

Widgets are responsible for presentation only.

Do not place the following inside widgets:
- API calls
- repository calls
- business rules
- authentication logic
- persistence logic
- complex validation
- business calculations
- data transformation unrelated to presentation

Do not put business logic inside build() methods.
Do not perform network calls directly from widgets.

Prefer small, focused widgets with one clear responsibility.

Extract a widget when it has a meaningful responsibility, it improves
readability, it is genuinely reused, or it isolates complex UI.
Do not extract every few lines into a widget.

Avoid deeply nested and unnecessarily large build methods.
Prefer composition over inheritance for UI.

Reusable widgets should not contain feature-specific business logic.
Reusable widgets should expose meaningful parameters instead of knowing about
specific feature implementations.
